{title: 648 - I Vow to Thee, My Country}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #648 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 648}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I[Eb]vow to [Ab]thee, my [Bb]country, all [Eb]earthly things [F]a[Gm]bove,
[Dm]En[Eb]tire and [Ab]whole and [Bb]perfect, the [Eb]service of my [Bb]love;
[Bb]The [F]love that [Gm]asks the [F]reason, [Bb]the [F]love that [Bb]stands the [Eb]test,
[Cm]That [Gm]lays up[Bb]on [Eb]the [Bb]al[Cm]tar [Bb]the [Eb]dearest [Cm]and [Gm]the [F]be[Gm]st;
[F]The [Eb]love that [Cm]never [Bb]falters, [Dm]the [Eb]love that pays [F]the [Gm]price,
[F]The [Eb]love that [Ab]makes [Bb]undaunted the [Eb]final sacri[Bb]fice.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]And [Eb]there's [Ab]another [Bb]country, I've [Eb]heard [F]of [Gm]long ago,
[Dm]Most dear [Eb]to them [Ab]that love [Bb]her, most [Eb]great to [Bb]them that know;
[Bb]We [F]may not [Gm]count [F]her armies, [Bb]we [F]may not [Bb]see [Eb]her King;
[Cm][Gm]Her [Bb]fortress [Eb]is [Bb]a [Cm]faithful [Bb][Eb]heart, [Cm]her [Gm]pride [F]is [Gm]suffering;
[F]And [Eb]one [Cm]by one [Bb]and [Dm]fervently [Eb]we pray [F]for [Gm]her increase,
[F]And her [Eb]ways are [Ab]ways of [Bb]gentleness, and [Eb]all her [Bb]paths are peace.
{end_of_verse}
